{"id":"c67a99fda9158bac","group":"58","path":"58/batch11/58-df-zfc-algebra2-ideal-generated.md","title":"ZFC Algebra2 Ideal Generated","display":"df-zfc-algebra2-ideal-generated — ZFC Algebra2 Ideal Generated","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-algebra2-ideal-generated","aliases":["58-df-zfc-algebra2-ideal-generated"],"display":"df-zfc-algebra2-ideal-generated — ZFC Algebra2 Ideal Generated","depends_on":["[[58-ax-zfc]]","[[58-df-ring]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-algebra2-ideal-generated"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-algebra2-ideal-generated</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-algebra2-ideal-generated — ZFC Algebra2 Ideal Generated"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" href=\"?note=a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" title=\"58-ax-zfc\">58-ax-zfc</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"1c30d21ea7b443f6\" href=\"?note=1c30d21ea7b443f6\" title=\"58-df-ring\">58-df-ring</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R,A,I\\in V\">\\(R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R,A,I\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Ring}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{Ring}_S\\)</span> (unital-ring predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"1c30d21ea7b443f6\" href=\"?note=1c30d21ea7b443f6\" title=\"58-df-ring\">58-df-ring</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\\subseteq R\">\\(A\\subseteq R\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcAlgebra2IdealGenerated}_S\\subseteq V^7\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcAlgebra2IdealGenerated}_S\\subseteq V^7\\)</span> (ring-relative predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}algebra2\\text{-}ideal\\text{-}generated} \\vdash \\mathrm{ZfcAlgebra2IdealGenerated}_S(I,A,R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R)\\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{Ring}_S(R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R)\\land A\\subseteq R\\land I=\\bigcap\\Bigl\\{J\\subseteq R\\mid A\\subseteq J\\land 0_R\\in J\\land\\forall x,y\\in J\\;(x-y\\in J)\\land\\forall r\\in R\\;\\forall x\\in J\\;(r\\cdot_Rx\\in J\\land x\\cdot_Rr\\in J)\\Bigr\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}algebra2\\text{-}ideal\\text{-}generated} \\vdash \\mathrm{ZfcAlgebra2IdealGenerated}_S(I,A,R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R)\\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{Ring}_S(R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R)\\land A\\subseteq R\\land I=\\bigcap\\Bigl\\{J\\subseteq R\\mid A\\subseteq J\\land 0_R\\in J\\land\\forall x,y\\in J\\;(x-y\\in J)\\land\\forall r\\in R\\;\\forall x\\in J\\;(r\\cdot_Rx\\in J\\land x\\cdot_Rr\\in J)\\Bigr\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The two-sided-ideal condition is expanded in the assertion; the undefined notation <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"J\\lhd R\">\\(J\\lhd R\\)</span> is no longer used as if it were a primitive predicate.</li>\n<li>The four ring-structure components are part of the predicate signature, so the generated ideal is not allowed to depend on hidden free operations on the same carrier.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-ax-zfc","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-ax-zfc]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-ring","status":"resolved","id":"1c30d21ea7b443f6","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-ring]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-ring","status":"resolved","id":"1c30d21ea7b443f6","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{Ring}_S$ (unital-ring predicate, see [[58-df-ring]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R,A,I\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Ring}_S","display":false},{"tex":"A\\subseteq R","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZfcAlgebra2IdealGenerated}_S\\subseteq V^7","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}algebra2\\text{-}ideal\\text{-}generated} \\vdash \\mathrm{ZfcAlgebra2IdealGenerated}_S(I,A,R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R)\\leftrightarrow \\operatorname{Ring}_S(R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R)\\land A\\subseteq R\\land I=\\bigcap\\Bigl\\{J\\subseteq R\\mid A\\subseteq J\\land 0_R\\in J\\land\\forall x,y\\in J\\;(x-y\\in J)\\land\\forall r\\in R\\;\\forall x\\in J\\;(r\\cdot_Rx\\in J\\land x\\cdot_Rr\\in J)\\Bigr\\}","display":true},{"tex":"J\\lhd R","display":false}],"bytes":1332,"backlinks":[{"id":"e85b3308cfc79da5","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1420","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch11/58-df-zfc-algebra2-ideal-generated.md|58-df-zfc-algebra2-ideal-generated]]（batch11）"}],"outgoing":["a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","1c30d21ea7b443f6"]}